    "body": "At this point re-reviewing this, I'm not sure I understand the point of this Note. It must be saying one of the following:\r\n\r\n1. That \"entry's URL\" and the \"non-fetch scheme document navigation params's URL\" can \"change\", as in \"get out-of-sync\"\r\n2. Or are they both changing (together), away from... what? From what they once were, before the redirect?\r\n3. Or literally the previous step (i.e., the call to \"attempt to create a non-fetch scheme document\") can change the entry's URL / navigation params's URL\r\n\r\n(1) seems impossible, and (3) doesn't seem to happen at all (we don't mutate the navigation params in that path, I think). So I think it's saying (2). But I'm not sure I understand why that's important to note here. For all redirects, [entry's URL changes, right](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#create-navigation-params-by-fetching:~:text=Set%20entry%27s%20URL%20to%20currentURL)? Why do we note that here specifically?",
