    "body": "I think it would be useful to elaborate on how this differs from the \"document is non-null\" signal, explicitly here. Maybe we could add a note saying:\r\n\r\n1. This is true in a strict subset of the cases where the document is non-null\r\n2. That is, there are some cases where the document is non-null (i.e., non-fetch scheme document & error cases.... those seem to be the only two?) and we _still_ don't want to persist data regarding that transient document to session history, which is what this document is for.",
