    "body": "Hmm yeah. I think it's probably not something we need to note here in this algorithm. We could add a note near the definition of \"hand-off to external software\" explaining that it has two possible call sites, non-fetch scheme navigations and fetch scheme navigations that end up unsupported. But I think we can do that separately from this PR, if we think it's a good idea.\r\n\r\n(In general I'm never sure whether documenting the call sites is that useful. We already have the reference boxes that show all the call sites, although they kind of get muddled with references and not just call sites. And there's a potential maintenance hazard, in theory. But maybe in this case it'd be useful...)",
